   "subject": "INLA survival model under-utilizes my hardware, how do I speed it up?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I am estimating a recurrent event survival model with INLA. I have several million observations, from which I am taking a sample. The size of the sample is going to be a function of the model estimation speed. I used the kidney dataset to get the syntax of the model (see below). After playing with the kidney example, I started using my own data. To improve the performance I spun up a Linux2 server on AWS with 16 cores and added these three options:<br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">num</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">threads </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">15</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> blas</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">num</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">threads </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">15</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> control</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">compute </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">openmp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">strategy </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;huge&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br><div>Originally, I only added the control.compute argument, but didn&#39;t see a huge change in performance. It looked like it was only using a single core. I tried adding the thread arguments, but it is basically running on a single core in the server environment. </div><div><br></div><div>Is there some option I am missing to speed this up?</div><div><br></div><div>Kidney example:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">formula </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inla</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">surv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">time</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">status</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> age </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sex  <br>        </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> f</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">id</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;iid&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> hyper </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prec </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">param</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br><br><br>kid</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">inla </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inla</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">formula</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> family</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;coxph&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">kidney</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                control</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hazard </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scale</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                num</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">threads </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></div></code></div><div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
